{"i": "For {proj}, '{goal}' adds an endpoint that reads and then writes. What decomposition keeps the transaction story safe?",
 "a": "Decompose the data work as a transactional unit first: model the read-modify-write with its race conditions, implement the atomic path with concurrency tests, then expose it through routing and validation. Transaction shape precedes route polish. Endpoints that interleave read-write without it are race farms."},
